now they must bear their guilt. 
Yahweh will demolish their altars; 
he will destroy their pillars.

Ephraim is a trained heifer that loves to thresh the grain, 
so I will put a yoke on her fair neck. 
I will put a yoke on Ephraim; 
Judah will plow; 
Jacob will pull the harrow by himself.

I will not execute my fierce anger; 
I will not again destroy Ephraim. 
For I am God 
and not a man; 
I am the Holy One among you, 
and I will not come in wrath.

Yahweh also has a lawsuit against Judah 
and will punish Jacob for what he has done; 
he will repay him for his deeds.

Jacob fled to the land of Aram; 
Israel worked in order to get a wife; 
and he kept flocks of sheep to get a wife.

But I am Yahweh your God from the land of Egypt. 
You must acknowledge no God but me; 
you must acknowledge that besides me, there is no other savior.

When you had pasture, then you became full; 
and when you were filled, your heart became lifted up. 
For that reason you forgot me.

“I will heal their turning away; 
I will love them freely, 
for my anger has turned away from him.

I will be like the dew to Israel; 
he will blossom like the lily 
and take root like a cedar in Lebanon.

His branches will spread out; 
his beauty will be like the olive trees, 
and his fragrance like the cedars in Lebanon.

What the swarming locust has left the great locust has eaten; 
what the great locust has left the grasshopper has eaten; 
and what the grasshopper has left the caterpillar has eaten.

Even the animals of the fields pant for you, 
for the water brooks have dried up, 
and fire has devoured the pastures of the wilderness.

They run like mighty warriors; 
they climb the walls like soldiers; 
they march, every one in step, 
and do not break their ranks.

Neither does one thrust another aside; 
they march, each in his path; 
they break through the defenses 
and do not fall out of line.

He said, “Yahweh will roar from Zion; 
he will raise his voice from Jerusalem. 
The pastures of the shepherds will dry up; 
the top of Carmel will wither.”

The swift will find no escape; 
the strong will not add to his own strength; 
neither will the mighty save himself.

The archer will not stand; 
the fast runner will not escape; 
the horseman will not save himself.

The lion has roared; 
who will not fear? 
The Lord Yahweh has spoken; 
who will not prophesy?

This is what Yahweh says: 
“As the shepherd rescues out of the mouth of the lion 
two legs only, or a piece of an ear; 
so will the people of Israel who live in Samaria be rescued; 
they will be left with only the corner of a couch 
or a piece of a bed.”

Offer a thanksgiving sacrifice with bread; 
proclaim freewill offerings; announce them, 
for this pleases you, 
you people of Israel 
—this is the declaration of the Lord Yahweh.

Therefore I will do something terrible to you, Israel; 
and because I will do something terrible to you, 
prepare to meet your God, Israel!

The virgin Israel has fallen; 
she will rise no more; 
she is forsaken on her land; 
there is no one to raise her up.

Do not seek Bethel; 
nor enter Gilgal; 
do not journey to Beersheba. 
For Gilgal will surely go into captivity, 
and Bethel will become nothing.

God made the Pleiades and Orion; 
he turns darkness into the morning; 
he makes the day dark with night 
and calls for the waters of the sea; 
he pours them out on the surface of the earth. 
Yahweh is his name!

Your leaders say, “Go to Kalneh and look; 
from there go to Hamath, the great city; 
then go down to Gath of the Philistines. 
Are they better than your two kingdoms? 
Is their border larger than your border?”

Therefore this is what Yahweh says, 'Your wife will be a prostitute in the city; 
your sons and your daughters will fall by the sword; 
your land will be measured and divided up; 
you will die in an unclean land, 
and Israel will surely go into exile from his land.'”

The Lord Yahweh of hosts 
touches the land and it melts; 
all who live in it mourn; 
all of it will rise up like the River, 
and sink again like the river of Egypt.

The waters closed around me up to my neck; 
the deep was all around me; 
seaweed wrapped around my head.

I went down to the bases of the mountains; 
the earth with its bars closed upon me forever. 
Yet you brought up my life from the pit, Yahweh, my God!

But as for me, I will sacrifice to you with a voice of thanksgiving; 
I will fulfill that which I have vowed. 
Salvation comes from Yahweh!”

Look, Yahweh comes out of his place; 
he will come down and tread 
on the high places of the earth.

For this reason I will lament and wail; 
I will go barefoot and naked; 
I will wail like the jackals 
and mourn like owls.

Do not tell about it in Gath; 
do not weep at all. 
At Beth Leaphrah I roll myself in the dust.

I will again bring a conqueror to you, 
inhabitants of Mareshah; 
the splendor of Israel will come to Adullam.

Get up and leave, 
for this is not a place where you can stay, 
because of its uncleanness; 
it is destroyed with complete destruction.

Now many nations are assembled against you; 
they say, 'Let her be defiled; 
let our eyes gloat over Zion.'

Now listen to what Yahweh says, 
“Arise and state your case before the mountains; 
let the hills hear your voice.

You will sow but not reap; 
you will tread the olives but not anoint yourselves with oil; 
you will press grapes but drink no wine.

Faithful people have disappeared from the land; 
there is no upright person in all mankind. 
They all lie in wait to shed blood; 
each one hunts his own brother with a net.

But as for me, I will look to Yahweh. 
I will wait for the God of my salvation; 
my God will hear me.

On that day your people will come to you, 
from Assyria and the cities in Egypt, 
from Egypt to the River, 
from sea to sea, 
and from mountain to mountain.

You will again have compassion on us; 
you will trample our iniquities under your feet. 
You will throw all our sins into the depths of the sea.

This is what Yahweh says, 
“Even if they are at their full strength and full numbers, they will nevertheless be sheared; 
their people will be no more. But you, Judah: Though I have afflicted you, I will afflict you no more.

Yet Thebes was carried away; she went into captivity; 
her young children were dashed in pieces at the head of every street; 
her enemies threw lots for her honorable men, 
and all her great men were bound in chains.

See, the people among you are women; 
the gates of your land have been opened wide to your enemies; 
fire has devoured their bars.

Go draw water for the siege; strengthen your fortresses; 
go into the clay and tread the mortar; 
pick up the molds for the bricks.

Your eyes are too pure to gaze upon evil, and you are not able to look on wrongdoing with favor; 
why then have you looked favorably on those who betray? 
Why are you silent while the wicked swallow up those more righteous than they are?

He brings all of them up with a fishhook; 
he drags men away in his fishnet; 
he gathers them together in his dragnet; 
so he rejoices and he is glad.

Yahweh, I have heard your report, and I am afraid. 
Yahweh, revive your work in the midst of these times; in the midst of these times make it known; 
remember to have compassion in your wrath.

Though the fig tree does not bud and there is no produce from the vines; 
and though the produce of the olive tree disappoints 
and the fields yield no food; 
and though the flock is cut off from the fold 
and there are no cattle in the stalls, this is what I will do.

The remnant of Israel will no longer commit injustice or speak lies, 
and no deceitful tongue will be found in their mouth; 
so they will graze and lie down, and no one will make them afraid.”

Yahweh your God is among you, a mighty one to save you. 
He will celebrate over you with joy; he will be silent over you in his love; 
he will be glad over you with a shout for joy.

You have sown much seed, but bring in little harvest; you eat but do not have enough; 
you drink but cannot get drunk. You wear clothes but cannot warm yourselves, 
and the wage earner earns money only to put it into a bag full of holes!

For seeds of peace will be sown; 
the climbing vine will give its fruit and the earth will give its produce; 
the skies will give their dew, 
for I will make the remnant of this people inherit all these things.

For household idols speak falsely; the diviners envision a lie; 
they tell deceitful dreams and give empty comfort, 
so they wander like sheep and suffer because there is no shepherd.

Then it will come about that throughout all the land—this is Yahweh's declaration— 
that two-thirds of it will be cut off! Those people will perish; 
only one-third will remain there.

He will not break any bruised reed; 
he will not quench any smoking flax, 
until he leads justice to victory,

The voice of one calling out in the wilderness, 
'Make ready the way of the Lord; 
make his paths straight.'”

Yes, and you, child, will be called a prophet of the Most High, 
for you will go before the face of the Lord to prepare his paths, 
to prepare people for his coming,

“For it is written in the Book of Psalms, 'Let his field be made desolate, 
and do not let even one person live there'; 
'Let someone else take his position of leadership.'

'Look, you despisers, and be astonished and then perish; 
For I am doing a work in your days, 
A work that you shall never believe, even if someone announces it to you.'”

'After these things I will return, 
and I will build again the tent of David, which has fallen down; 
I will set up and restore its ruins again,

For it is written, “Rejoice, you barren one who does not give birth; 
cry out and shout for joy, you who are not suffering the pains of childbirth; 
because the children of the abandoned woman are more numerous 
than those of the woman who has a husband.”
